With redispatch available (@tab-cong):

- *both relaxations stay exact* under congestion;
- the AC gap is at most $2 times 10^(-9)$;
- ADMM converges in 45-57 iterations to within $1.2 times 10^(-3)$-$2.2 times 10^(-3)$ \$/MWh of the monolithic prices;
- the boundary identity $-lambda_p = pi_(P,3) dot 100$ holds to the printed digits.

The prices behave as expected:

- line congestion splits the transmission prices: node 1 falls to 56.81 \$/MWh and equals $2 c_2 P_g + c_1$; node 2 rises to 68.43 \$/MWh, equal to G2's marginal cost;
- head congestion makes the DG marginal: node 6 is priced at exactly 70.00 \$/MWh.

