On the transmission side the SDP balances are written in $W$ (traces $"Tr"(Phi_k W)$), not as radial branch flows, so the radial path-sum decomposition does not apply. The script reports three quantities there:

- the reference price at node 1, which equals $2 c_2 P_g + c_1$ in every variant;
- the shadow price of the binding line;
- the nodal spreads, e.g. $pi_(P,2) - pi_(P,1) = 11.6133$ \$/MWh under line congestion.

